{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-1925","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1861","text":"[&] / CC2 — Capability Composition, v2 (Coalitional)"}]},{"id":"blk-1926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1862","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-1863","text":" Draft · "},{"id":"spn-1864","marks":["bold"],"text":"Replaces:"},{"id":"spn-1865","text":" CC1 (single-agent "},{"id":"spn-1866","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-1867","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1868","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-1869","text":" composition) · "},{"id":"spn-1870","marks":["bold"],"text":"Depends on:"},{"id":"spn-1871","text":" "},{"id":"spn-1872","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-1873","text":" ≥ 0.8 (the eight-rung modality ladder)"}]},{"id":"blk-1927","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1874","text":"The key words MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, and MAY are to be interpreted as in RFC 2119."}]},{"id":"blk-1928","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1875","text":"0. Abstract"}]},{"id":"blk-1929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1876","text":"CC1 formalized composition for a "},{"id":"spn-1877","marks":["italic"],"text":"single"},{"id":"spn-1878","text":" agent: a capability "},{"id":"spn-1879","marks":["bold"],"text":"set"},{"id":"spn-1880","text":" merged by an associative-commutative-idempotent "},{"id":"spn-1881","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-1882","text":", data flowed through a "},{"id":"spn-1883","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-1884","text":" pipeline, and a flat governance block of "},{"id":"spn-1885","marks":["code"],"text":"hard"},{"id":"spn-1886","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1887","marks":["code"],"text":"soft"},{"id":"spn-1888","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1889","marks":["code"],"text":"escalate_when"},{"id":"spn-1890","text":" constraints rode alongside. CC1 gave "},{"id":"spn-1891","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-1892","text":" an algebra (a bounded join-semilattice — the CRDT laws) but left "},{"id":"spn-1893","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-1894","text":" "},{"id":"spn-1895","marks":["bold"],"text":"lawless"},{"id":"spn-1896","text":" and treated compatibility, governance, and self-evolution as side-conditions checked outside the algebra."}]},{"id":"blk-1930","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1897","text":"CC2 makes two changes. First, it gives every part of composition a "},{"id":"spn-1898","marks":["bold"],"text":"semantics"},{"id":"spn-1899","text":" drawn from the arithmetic ladder, including the previously-lawless "},{"id":"spn-1900","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-1901","text":". Second, it lifts composition from one agent to a "},{"id":"spn-1902","marks":["bold"],"text":"coalition"},{"id":"spn-1903","text":", so the question composition answers is no longer "},{"id":"spn-1904","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"do I hold these capabilities?\""},{"id":"spn-1905","text":" but *\"can this group, by pooling typed capabilities and coordinating, "},{"id":"spn-1906","marks":["bold"],"text":"ensure"},{"id":"spn-1907","text":" the goal — with each task owned, the shared facts common knowledge, the joint run supervised, and a safety floor none of them can weaken?\"* Every clause of that sentence is a rung."}]},{"id":"blk-1931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1908","text":"CC2 is normative at the level of "},{"id":"spn-1909","marks":["italic"],"text":"the verdict"},{"id":"spn-1910","text":": two conformant runtimes, in any language, MUST agree on whether a composition is feasible, permitted, and ensurable, because the verdict is the arithmetic and the arithmetic is fixed by its laws (the conformance suite; run it for the count — "},{"id":"spn-1911","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/laws.mjs && node test/compose-laws.mjs"},{"id":"spn-1912","text":" derives "},{"id":"spn-1913","marks":["bold"],"text":"210 enforced"},{"id":"spn-1914","text":", 109 kernel + 101 compose, plus 3 declared-open). The runtime, the syntax, and the transport are not normative; an effects-first Elixir runtime — "},{"id":"spn-1915","marks":["bold"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-1916","text":" — is one conformant host, a TypeScript edge runtime another."}]},{"id":"blk-1932","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1917","text":"1. The shift, in one table"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-1934","spans":[{"id":"spn-1918","text":"CC1 (single agent)"}]},{"id":"blk-1935","spans":[{"id":"spn-1919","text":"CC2 (coalition)"}]},{"id":"blk-1936","spans":[{"id":"spn-1920","text":"Rung"}]}],"id":"blk-1933","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-1937","spans":[{"id":"spn-1921","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-1922","text":" merges "},{"id":"spn-1923","marks":["italic"],"text":"my"},{"id":"spn-1924","text":" capability set"}]},{"id":"blk-1938","spans":[{"id":"spn-1925","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-1926","text":" merges the coalition's "},{"id":"spn-1927","marks":["bold"],"text":"joint"},{"id":"spn-1928","text":" capability set, tagged by holder"}]},{"id":"blk-1939","spans":[{"id":"spn-1929","text":"alethic (lattice)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1940","spans":[{"id":"spn-1930","text":"`\\"}]},{"id":"blk-1941","spans":[{"id":"spn-1931","text":">` flows data (no laws)"}]},{"id":"blk-1942","spans":[{"id":"spn-1932","text":"`\\"}]},{"id":"blk-1943","spans":[{"id":"spn-1933","text":">` is a "},{"id":"spn-1934","marks":["bold"],"text":"governed sequential pipeline"},{"id":"spn-1935","text":" spanning agents"}]},{"id":"blk-1944","spans":[{"id":"spn-1936","text":"alethic "},{"id":"spn-1937","marks":["code"],"text":"chain"},{"id":"spn-1938","text":" + heuristic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1945","spans":[{"id":"spn-1939","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-1940","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1941","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-1942","text":" checked at validation"}]},{"id":"blk-1946","spans":[{"id":"spn-1943","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-1944","marks":["bold"],"text":"feasibility gate"},{"id":"spn-1945","text":": incompatible hand-offs annihilate to "},{"id":"spn-1946","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"}]},{"id":"blk-1947","spans":[{"id":"spn-1947","text":"alethic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1948","spans":[{"id":"spn-1948","marks":["code"],"text":"cost"},{"id":"spn-1949","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1950","marks":["code"],"text":"confidence"},{"id":"spn-1951","text":" as config thresholds"}]},{"id":"blk-1949","spans":[{"id":"spn-1952","text":"end-to-end quantities "},{"id":"spn-1953","marks":["bold"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-1954","text":" along the pipeline"}]},{"id":"blk-1950","spans":[{"id":"spn-1955","text":"axiological (semiring)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1951","spans":[{"id":"spn-1956","marks":["code"],"text":"hard"},{"id":"spn-1957","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1958","marks":["code"],"text":"soft"},{"id":"spn-1959","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-1960","marks":["code"],"text":"escalate_when"},{"id":"spn-1961","text":" (flat list)"}]},{"id":"blk-1952","spans":[{"id":"spn-1962","marks":["bold"],"text":"floor / gradient / contrary-to-duty"},{"id":"spn-1963","text":", composed and resolved"}]},{"id":"blk-1953","spans":[{"id":"spn-1964","text":"deontic + bridge"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1954","spans":[{"id":"spn-1965","text":"— (no notion)"}]},{"id":"blk-1955","spans":[{"id":"spn-1966","text":"each task has an "},{"id":"spn-1967","marks":["bold"],"text":"owner"},{"id":"spn-1968","text":" obligated for it"}]},{"id":"blk-1956","spans":[{"id":"spn-1969","text":"deontic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1957","spans":[{"id":"spn-1970","text":"—"}]},{"id":"blk-1958","spans":[{"id":"spn-1971","text":"safety + liveness over the "},{"id":"spn-1972","marks":["bold"],"text":"joint trajectory"}]},{"id":"blk-1959","spans":[{"id":"spn-1973","text":"temporal (supervise)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1960","spans":[{"id":"spn-1974","marks":["code"],"text":"requires_approval"},{"id":"spn-1975","text":" for mutations"}]},{"id":"blk-1961","spans":[{"id":"spn-1976","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-1977","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared entrenched floor"},{"id":"spn-1978","text":" no agent or coalition can weaken"}]},{"id":"blk-1962","spans":[{"id":"spn-1979","text":"reflexive"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1963","spans":[{"id":"spn-1980","text":"—"}]},{"id":"blk-1964","spans":[{"id":"spn-1981","text":"coordination requires "},{"id":"spn-1982","marks":["bold"],"text":"common knowledge"},{"id":"spn-1983","text":" of the plan"}]},{"id":"blk-1965","spans":[{"id":"spn-1984","text":"epistemic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-1966","spans":[{"id":"spn-1985","text":"—"}]},{"id":"blk-1967","spans":[{"id":"spn-1986","text":"the coalition "},{"id":"spn-1987","marks":["bold"],"text":"can ensure"},{"id":"spn-1988","text":" the goal vs. any adversary"}]},{"id":"blk-1968","spans":[{"id":"spn-1989","text":"strategic"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-1969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1990","text":"CC1 is the special case of CC2 where the coalition is a singleton and the adversary is empty."}]},{"id":"blk-1970","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1991","text":"2. The two operators, lifted"}]},{"id":"blk-1971","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1992","text":"2.1 "},{"id":"spn-1993","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-1994","text":" — composition (join-semilattice, with holders)"}]},{"id":"blk-1972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1995","marks":["code"],"text":"A & B"},{"id":"spn-1996","text":" MUST be associative, commutative, and idempotent with identity "},{"id":"spn-1997","marks":["code"],"text":"&none"},{"id":"spn-1998","text":" (unchanged from CC1 — these are the CRDT convergence laws and they are what let independent agents compose to the same set). CC2 adds that each capability in the joint set carries its "},{"id":"spn-1999","marks":["bold"],"text":"holder"},{"id":"spn-2000","text":" (the agent that provides it) and its "},{"id":"spn-2001","marks":["bold"],"text":"contract"},{"id":"spn-2002","text":" (its "},{"id":"spn-2003","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-2004","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-2005","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-2006","text":" types). The merge is the lattice join of capability sets; the holder tag is provenance, not a tiebreak, so idempotence is preserved."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2007","text":"Conformance: "},{"id":"spn-2008","marks":["code"],"text":"A & B == B & A"},{"id":"spn-2009","text":", "},{"id":"spn-2010","marks":["code"],"text":"(A & B) & C == A & (B & C)"},{"id":"spn-2011","text":", "},{"id":"spn-2012","marks":["code"],"text":"A & A == A"},{"id":"spn-2013","text":", "},{"id":"spn-2014","marks":["code"],"text":"A & none == A"},{"id":"spn-2015","text":". (Arith: the "},{"id":"spn-2016","marks":["code"],"text":"sigma"},{"id":"spn-2017","text":" join-semilattice family; laws of the lattice.)"}]}],"id":"blk-1973","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-1975","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2018","text":"2.2 "},{"id":"spn-2019","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-2020","text":" — pipeline (sequential monoid, governed)"}]},{"id":"blk-1976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2021","text":"This is the operator CC1 left undefined. In CC2, "},{"id":"spn-2022","marks":["code"],"text":"X |> f"},{"id":"spn-2023","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-2024","marks":["bold"],"text":"sequential composition"},{"id":"spn-2025","text":": order matters, it is associative, and the empty pipeline (pass-through context) is its identity. It is "},{"id":"spn-2026","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-2027","text":" commutative and "},{"id":"spn-2028","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-2029","text":" idempotent. This is exactly the invariant layer's "},{"id":"spn-2030","marks":["code"],"text":"chain"},{"id":"spn-2031","text":", phase-graded, with the provenance hash-chain as its trace."}]},{"id":"blk-1977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2032","text":"Two things ride on the pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-1978","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2033","marks":["bold"],"text":"Feasibility."},{"id":"spn-2034","text":" At each hand-off, the producer's "},{"id":"spn-2035","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-2036","text":" MUST be compatible with the consumer's "},{"id":"spn-2037","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-2038","text":", or the composed value is infeasible — it carries "},{"id":"spn-2039","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-2040","text":", which annihilates through the pipeline (arith: the alethic "},{"id":"spn-2041","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-2042","text":" gate). A type-incompatible pipeline does not \"fail validation\"; it "},{"id":"spn-2043","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-2044","text":" the zero of the composition."}]}],"id":"blk-1979","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2045","marks":["bold"],"text":"Quantities."},{"id":"spn-2046","text":" Cost, confidence, and latency compose end-to-end through the pipeline via a semiring (arith: heuristic). Confidence as a product, cost as a sum, worst-case latency as a max. A runtime MUST NOT treat "},{"id":"spn-2047","marks":["code"],"text":"confidence_below"},{"id":"spn-2048","text":" as a fixed config constant; it is the composed quantity compared against the consuming step's "},{"id":"spn-2049","marks":["code"],"text":"requires"},{"id":"spn-2050","text":" threshold (the epistemic β-gate)."}]}],"id":"blk-1981","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2051","text":"Conformance: "},{"id":"spn-2052","marks":["code"],"text":"(X |> f) |> g == X |> (f |> g)"},{"id":"spn-2053","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-2054","marks":["code"],"text":"X |> id == X"},{"id":"spn-2055","text":"; an infeasible stage yields "},{"id":"spn-2056","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-2057","text":" for the whole pipeline."}]}],"id":"blk-1983","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-1985","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2058","text":"3. The Coalition object"}]},{"id":"blk-1986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2059","text":"A composition in CC2 is a "},{"id":"spn-2060","marks":["bold"],"text":"coalition"},{"id":"spn-2061","text":": a set of agents, a goal, and the governance that binds them. It is to CC2 what "},{"id":"spn-2062","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-2063","text":" is to CC1, one level up. (Schema shown as a sketch; the canonical form is left to the wire annex.)"}]},{"id":"blk-1987","kind":"code","language":"jsonc","text":"{\n  \"coalition\": \"ship_it\",\n  \"agents\": [\"dev\", \"qa\", \"ops\"],          // who is in the coalition\n  \"ensure\": \"deployed AND tests_pass\",      // strategic: the goal the coalition must be ABLE to force\n  \"common_knowledge\": [\"release_plan\",      // epistemic: facts that MUST be common knowledge to coordinate\n                       \"rollback_ready\"],\n  \"owns\": {                                  // deontic: every task has exactly one obligated owner\n    \"dev\": \"build\", \"qa\": \"verify\", \"ops\": \"release\"\n  },\n  \"shield\": [\"NEVER secrets_leaked\"],        // temporal: safety over the JOINT trajectory\n  \"floor\": [\"entrench: no_prod_without_qa\"], // reflexive: un-weakenable, even under learning\n  \"compose\": \"build |> verify |> release\"    // the cross-agent pipeline (the lifted |>)\n}"},{"id":"blk-1988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2064","text":"A coalition is "},{"id":"spn-2065","marks":["bold"],"text":"admissible"},{"id":"spn-2066","text":" iff (arith, all checked):"}]},{"id":"blk-1989","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1991","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2067","marks":["bold"],"text":"(strategic)"},{"id":"spn-2068","text":" the coalition "},{"id":"spn-2069","marks":["code"],"text":"canEnsure"},{"id":"spn-2070","text":" the goal against the worst case of any non-member: "},{"id":"spn-2071","marks":["code"],"text":"⟨⟨agents⟩⟩◊ ensure"},{"id":"spn-2072","text":". If not, the coalition MUST NOT be enacted as-is; it escalates (recruit agents, or weaken the goal). This is "},{"id":"spn-2073","marks":["italic"],"text":"ought-implies-can"},{"id":"spn-2074","text":": you may not bind a coalition to a goal it cannot force."}]}],"id":"blk-1990","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1993","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2075","marks":["bold"],"text":"(epistemic)"},{"id":"spn-2076","text":" every fact in "},{"id":"spn-2077","marks":["code"],"text":"common_knowledge"},{"id":"spn-2078","text":" is common knowledge among "},{"id":"spn-2079","marks":["code"],"text":"agents"},{"id":"spn-2080","text":". A joint strategy that depends on a fact some member does not commonly know is not executable (the coordinated-attack result). The runtime's broadcast mechanism is what "},{"id":"spn-2081","marks":["italic"],"text":"establishes"},{"id":"spn-2082","text":" common knowledge; CC2 only requires that it has been established before the pipeline runs."}]}],"id":"blk-1992","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1995","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2083","marks":["bold"],"text":"(deontic)"},{"id":"spn-2084","text":" "},{"id":"spn-2085","marks":["code"],"text":"owns"},{"id":"spn-2086","text":" is a total function from tasks to a single agent. No task may be unowned (responsibility diffusion is forbidden) and conflicting obligations between agents are resolved by the deontic "},{"id":"spn-2087","marks":["code"],"text":"resolve"},{"id":"spn-2088","text":" (priority) before enactment."}]}],"id":"blk-1994","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1997","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2089","marks":["bold"],"text":"(temporal)"},{"id":"spn-2090","text":" the joint trajectory the "},{"id":"spn-2091","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-2092","text":" pipeline can produce satisfies the "},{"id":"spn-2093","marks":["code"],"text":"shield"},{"id":"spn-2094","text":" safety formulas; a reachable violation makes the coalition inadmissible. Liveness goals ("},{"id":"spn-2095","marks":["code"],"text":"F good"},{"id":"spn-2096","text":") that fail only at the horizon become coalition-level obligations with contrary-to-duty escalation."}]}],"id":"blk-1996","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1999","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2097","marks":["bold"],"text":"(reflexive)"},{"id":"spn-2098","text":" the "},{"id":"spn-2099","marks":["code"],"text":"floor"},{"id":"spn-2100","text":" constraints are entrenched; no later amendment by any agent or sub-coalition can weaken them. The coalition MAY revise everything else (and SHOULD, as it learns); it MUST NOT weaken the floor."}]}],"id":"blk-1998","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-2000","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2101","text":"4. The macro layer (DSL → arith)"}]},{"id":"blk-2001","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2102","text":"Composition SHOULD be written in a host DSL whose keywords compile to arith operations. The DSL is sugar; each keyword MUST have the documented expansion below, so the surface is readable but the semantics are exactly the verdict engine. (Syntax shown in an Elixir-macro style targeting an effects-first runtime; the bodies — "},{"id":"spn-2103","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-2104","text":", "},{"id":"spn-2105","marks":["code"],"text":"gather_evidence"},{"id":"spn-2106","text":", "},{"id":"spn-2107","marks":["code"],"text":"emit_event"},{"id":"spn-2108","text":" — are ordinary runtime effects, gated by an interpositional "},{"id":"spn-2109","marks":["code"],"text":"govern"},{"id":"spn-2110","text":" stage the runtime MUST run before any consequential effect.)"}]},{"id":"blk-2002","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2111","text":"4.1 Single governed agent"}]},{"id":"blk-2003","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule Researcher do\n  use BoxAndBox.Agent, name: :researcher\n  use BoxAndBox.Governed                   # adds the verdict layer over the effect engine\n\n  agent :researcher do\n    capability :search,\n      requires: knows(:query_valid),        # alethic feasibility ⊗ epistemic.knows\n      cost: 2, confidence: 0.9              # heuristic semiring weights\n  end\n\n  behavior :answer, triggers_on: [:query] do\n    govern do\n      hard      must_cite_sources()         # the floor — violate ⇒ infeasible (→ 0̲)\n      prefer    low_cost()                  # the gradient — ranks only feasible options\n      escalate  when: confidence_below(0.7) # contrary-to-duty → route :deliberate\n    end\n    sequence do                             # plain runtime effects, now gated\n      gather_evidence()\n      deliberate when: known_unknown(:answer)   # epistemic.knowsItDoesntKnow → :deliberate\n      emit_event :result, confidence: belief(:answer)\n    end\n  end\nend"},{"id":"blk-2004","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2112","text":"4.2 Coalition (the reworked CC)"}]},{"id":"blk-2005","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"coalition :ship_it, agents: [:dev, :qa, :ops] do\n  ensure deployed() and tests_pass()              # strategic.canEnsure (⟨⟨agents⟩⟩◊)\n  common_knowledge [:release_plan, :rollback_ready] # epistemic.common\n  owns :dev, &build/1                             # deontic OBLIGATORY, owner = :dev\n  owns :qa,  &verify/1\n  owns :ops, &release/1\n  shield never(secrets_leaked())                  # temporal.supervise safety over the joint run\n  floor  entrench(no_prod_without_qa())           # reflexive.entrench (un-weakenable)\n  compose build() |> verify() |> release()        # the lifted, governed |>\nend"},{"id":"blk-2006","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2113","text":"4.3 Expansion table (normative)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-2008","spans":[{"id":"spn-2114","text":"DSL keyword"}]},{"id":"blk-2009","spans":[{"id":"spn-2115","text":"Arith operation"}]},{"id":"blk-2010","spans":[{"id":"spn-2116","text":"Rung"}]}],"id":"blk-2007","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-2011","spans":[{"id":"spn-2117","marks":["code"],"text":"requires: φ"}]},{"id":"blk-2012","spans":[{"id":"spn-2118","marks":["code"],"text":"value.consume"},{"id":"spn-2119","text":" gate ⊗ "},{"id":"spn-2120","marks":["code"],"text":"epistemic.knows(φ)"}]},{"id":"blk-2013","spans":[{"id":"spn-2121","text":"alethic + epistemic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-2014","spans":[{"id":"spn-2122","marks":["code"],"text":"cost: / confidence: / latency:"}]},{"id":"blk-2015","spans":[{"id":"spn-2123","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-2124","text":" weights in the chosen semiring, composed along `\\"}]},{"id":"blk-2016","spans":[{"id":"spn-2125","text":">`"}]},{"id":"blk-2017","spans":[{"id":"spn-2126","text":"axiological"}]}],[{"id":"blk-2018","spans":[{"id":"spn-2127","marks":["code"],"text":"hard φ"}]},{"id":"blk-2019","spans":[{"id":"spn-2128","marks":["code"],"text":"norm"},{"id":"spn-2129","text":" "},{"id":"spn-2130","marks":["code"],"text":"FORBIDDEN(¬φ)"},{"id":"spn-2131","text":" placed on the floor; violation ⇒ "},{"id":"spn-2132","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"}]},{"id":"blk-2020","spans":[{"id":"spn-2133","text":"deontic + alethic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-2021","spans":[{"id":"spn-2134","marks":["code"],"text":"prefer φ"},{"id":"spn-2135","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-2136","marks":["code"],"text":"soft φ"}]},{"id":"blk-2022","spans":[{"id":"spn-2137","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-2138","text":" gradient term (semiring)"}]},{"id":"blk-2023","spans":[{"id":"spn-2139","text":"axiological"}]}],[{"id":"blk-2024","spans":[{"id":"spn-2140","marks":["code"],"text":"escalate when: C"}]},{"id":"blk-2025","spans":[{"id":"spn-2141","marks":["code"],"text":"govern"},{"id":"spn-2142","text":" contrary-to-duty → "},{"id":"spn-2143","marks":["code"],"text":"route :deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-2026","spans":[{"id":"spn-2144","text":"deontic (bridge)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-2027","spans":[{"id":"spn-2145","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate when: known_unknown(x)"}]},{"id":"blk-2028","spans":[{"id